    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d130">

                <pb facs="0219" n="115" sameAs="frus:frus1932v03/pg115"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/3711: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Shanghai (Cunningham) to the
                        Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-01-30T10:00:00+08:00">January 30, 1932—10
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received January 30—1 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Following to the Legation: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>Your January 29, 3 p.m.,<anchor n="83" xml:id="d130-f1"/> last paragraph.
                            Suggestion made by Japanese staff officer to Secretary General of
                            Council reported in my telegram of January 28, 2 p.m. is not favorably
                            considered by Council. I shall, however, carry out Legation’s
                            instructions.</p></quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Cunningham</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d130-f1" n="83" xml:id="d130-f1-content">
                <p>See telegram No. 148, January 29, 5 p.m., to the Department from the Minister in
                    China, <ref target="#pg97">p. 97</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
